message: "If you use this software or its evaluation data, please cite it as below."
title: "Pipeline Triage Agent"
abstract: >-
  An LLM-assisted triage tool for Apache Airflow pipeline failures. It reads a
  failed task's logs, classifies the root cause, and may open a pull request
  with a suggested fix — but only when the root cause is one a repository change
  can actually address. Ships with a local harness that reproduces fifteen
  realistic pipeline failures, and with the data from a 1,350-diagnosis evaluation
  across three models and three versions of the agent: the original prompt,
  specific root-cause guidance in the prompt, and a structural root-cause field
  with a server-side gate. Every pull request offered for a failure no code
  change can fix was applied and its pipeline re-run.
